"""
Ideal per-circuit ABS modulator: the ECU commands the wheel-side pressure it allows, and the valve
makes the caliper follow it after the solenoid lag `T_v`, never above the master-cylinder
pressure.

Ports: `port_a` the master-cylinder side; `port_b` the brake-line and caliper side; `p_cmd` the
allowed wheel-circuit pressure, gauge.

With p_a and p_b the two sides' gauge pressures, a command at or above p_a asks for the inlet
open, one below it for the inlet closed. The inlet's opening y, 1 open and 0 closed, follows that
request with the lag `T_v`, and the held pressure p_hold follows the command clamped to
[0, p_a], also with `T_v`:

    p_b = min(p_a, y p_a + (1 - y) p_hold)

So a valve held open passes p_a straight through, a closed one holds or dumps the wheel side to
the command, and both the close and the re-apply after it take the solenoid's time. The wheel side
never rises above p_a: when p_a falls below the held pressure, the inlet valve's parallel check
valve opens and the wheel side follows p_a down.

Fluid passes between the ports, either way, while the inlet is asked open or the check valve
conducts (p_hold >= p_a). Otherwise the closed valve still lets the caliper fill from the master
cylinder, and fluid dumped from the caliper goes where `return_dump` decides. At 0 it leaves the
model, so the master cylinder makes up every dumped volume and the pedal creeps forward without
pulsing. At 1 it re-enters at `port_a`, as if an ideal return pump with no accumulator pushed it
straight back to the master cylinder: the pedal is pushed back with every dump, the pulsation a
driver feels. `m_dump` is the fluid that leaves the model.

Pressures are gauge: the ports carry `p_amb` + p (`VehicleComponents.DOT4` has the convention).

Assumptions: the valve has no flow restriction and no volume of its own; it starts open, y = 1, with
the held pressure at 0. A start with the valve closed sets both at the declaration, `ABSValve(y =
initial 0.0, p_hold = initial 8e6)`. `T_v` lumps the electronics' and the solenoid's reaction
(assumed).
"""
component ABSValve
  "Master-cylinder side"
  port_a = HydraulicComponents.Interfaces.Port() {^port_a}
  "Brake-line and caliper side"
  port_b = HydraulicComponents.Interfaces.Port() {^port_b}
  "Allowed wheel-circuit pressure, gauge; at or above the master-cylinder side the inlet opens"
  p_cmd = RealInput() {^p_cmd}
  "Electronics and solenoid reaction time"
  parameter T_v::Time(min = eps(Float64)) = 0.03
  "Dumped fluid: 0 leaves the model, 1 returns to the master-cylinder side"
  parameter return_dump::Real = 0.0
  "Ambient pressure, which a released circuit sits at"
  parameter p_amb::Pressure = 100325.0
  "Master-cylinder side pressure, gauge"
  variable p_a::Pressure
  "Wheel side pressure, gauge"
  variable p_b::Pressure
  "Inlet opening: 1 open, 0 closed"
  variable y::Real = initial 1.0
  "Pressure the closed valve holds the wheel side at, gauge"
  variable p_hold::Pressure = initial 0.0
  "Command clamped to the master-cylinder side"
  variable p_target::Pressure
  "Mass flow of dumped fluid leaving the model"
  variable m_dump::MassFlowRate
relations
  continuity(port_a.medium, port_b.medium)
  port_a.p = p_amb + p_a
  port_b.p = p_amb + p_b
  p_target = min(max(p_cmd, 0.0), max(p_a, 0.0))
  der(p_hold) = (p_target - p_hold) / T_v
  der(y) = (ifelse(p_cmd >= p_a, 1.0, 0.0) - y) / T_v
  p_b = min(p_a, y * p_a + (1.0 - y) * p_hold)
  port_a.m_flow = ifelse(p_cmd >= p_a or p_hold >= p_a, -port_b.m_flow, max(-port_b.m_flow, 0.0) - return_dump * max(port_b.m_flow, 0.0))
  m_dump = port_a.m_flow + port_b.m_flow
metadata {
  "Dyad": {"icons": {"default": "dyad://VehicleComponents/Chassis/Brakes/ABSValve.svg"}},
  "_links": {
    "port_a": {
      "Dyad": {"placement": {"icon": {"iconName": "hydraulic_port_a", "x1": -50, "x2": 50, "y1": 450, "y2": 550}}}
    },
    "port_b": {
      "Dyad": {"placement": {"icon": {"iconName": "hydraulic_port_b", "x1": 950, "x2": 1050, "y1": 450, "y2": 550}}}
    },
    "p_cmd": {
      "Dyad": {"placement": {"icon": {"x1": 450, "x2": 550, "y1": 950, "y2": 1050, "rot": 270}}}
    }
  }
}
end
